# The conda env lives inside the project so it stays off the C: drive, which has
# under 10 GB free. It is 5+ GB and must never be committed.
.venv/
.hf/

# Generated: caches, checkpoints, run outputs. results/ keeps its structure via
# .gitkeep but not its contents -- an embedding cache is gigabytes and a rerun
# reproduces it from the config.
results/**
!results/.gitkeep

# ...except the small summary tables. The frozen-LaBSE baseline and the
# reconstruction ceiling are reference numbers that every later result is
# interpreted against, and they cost hours of GPU time to regenerate. Versioning
# them next to the code that produced them is the difference between "the model
# scored 0.72" and "the model scored 0.72 against a baseline of 0.9163 measured
# on this commit". A few kilobytes each.
#
# The directory rule is needed as well as the file rule: git will not descend
# into an excluded directory, so !results/*/*.json alone matches nothing.
!results/*/
!results/*/*.json
!results/*/*.yaml
# Figures too: the trade curve is Milestone 3's stated deliverable, and at ~73 KB
# it costs less than the paragraph needed to describe it. Checkpoints stay out --
# those are 3-10 MB each and a rerun reproduces them from the config.
!results/*/*.png

# The cache is the exception to the exception: corpus.json is 42 MB and
# vectors.f16 is 368 MB, and both are regenerated by scripts/stage_a.py.
results/cache/**

# Smoke output is synthetic. It proves the pipeline runs and nothing else, and
# the README says its numbers must never appear in a results table -- so keeping
# it out of the repo is consistent with that rather than trusting the filename
# to warn everyone who finds it.
results/smoke/**
*.f16
*.pt
*.npy
*.npz

__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
